        "text_gcWm8i": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Everything is patterned and sewn in Portland, Oregon, under a pattern-maker with thirty years in the trade.</p><p>We make one garment at a time, after you order it. It takes longer. In exchange, nothing sits in a warehouse waiting to be marked down, and nothing gets thrown out because we guessed wrong about how many people wanted a 32.</p><p>When something about a garment is wrong, we change it, and the number moves. CJ.101.<strong>1</strong> becomes CJ.101.<strong>2</strong>. The pair you own stays the pair you own — we just stop making that version. Most of the changes are small enough that only we would notice.</p><p>Every garment gets looked at on its way through the line. When one comes off wrong, we lose one.</p><p>If you need a size we don't list, or a length we don't cut, ask. Sometimes the answer is yes.</p><p>The studio is in Portland. If you're nearby, come by.</p>"
          }
        }
